Jenkins (biss-cicd): add 2 "Secret file" credentials for the Playwright test pipeline
Background
The BISS / ENTS automated regression suite has been migrated from Selenium to Playwright.
Repository: GitLab biss/biss-automation/dafm-automation_playwright
Branch: feature/playwright-migration
Jenkins: jenkins-biss-cicd > biss > biss/biss-automation/dafm-automation_playwright

The pipeline is set up and working up to the test step: Jenkins finds pipeline/Jenkinsfile,
the agent pod starts in namespace biss-cicd, and the code is cloned.
The run then stops with:
  CredentialNotFoundException: Could not find credentials entry with ID 'biss-playwright-db-properties'

The tests need two configuration files that contain passwords:
  - db.properties  (Oracle test database connection)
  - TestData.xlsx  (test user logins)
For security these files are NOT stored in GitLab. The Jenkinsfile reads them from Jenkins
Credentials at run time, copies them in for the duration of the test run and deletes them
straight afterwards. They are never printed to the log or archived.

My Jenkins account has no Credentials permission, so I cannot add them myself.

Request (either option is fine)
Option A - please add two credentials in the folder store of
           biss/biss-automation/dafm-automation_playwright (or the biss folder):
    1. Kind: Secret file   ID: biss-playwright-db-properties   Description: BISS Playwright db.properties
    2. Kind: Secret file   ID: biss-playwright-testdata        Description: BISS Playwright TestData
    The IDs must match exactly (lower case, no spaces) - they are referenced in pipeline/Jenkinsfile.
Option B - grant Aniket.Pathare Credentials Create / Update / View permission on the folder
           biss/biss-automation/dafm-automation_playwright, so the test team can add them and keep
           them up to date when test passwords change.

Handover of the files
The files contain passwords and will NOT be attached to this ticket or sent by email / Teams.
I will upload them directly during a short screen-share, or through whichever secure channel
Operations prefers.

Acceptance criteria
- Both credential IDs exist and are visible to the dafm-automation_playwright pipeline.
- A "Build with Parameters" run (TESTCASE_IDS = TC_00_DATA,TC_01_Login) gets past the
  credentials step; the console shows "Secret files copied (db.properties, TestData.xlsx)."

Reference
Jenkins build #4 on feature/playwright-migration (console output shows the error above).
